# Notifications API

## Route
- Gateway: `/api/notifications/{**catch-all}` → `srv-notification`
- Base path: `/api/notifications/v1`

## Endpoints
Prefix: `/api/notifications/v1/organizations/{organizationId}`

- `GET /` → `200 OK`; JWT required
  - Response: array of `{ id, type, title, body, organizationId, createdAt, isRead }`
  - Filtered by JWT `sub` (user id) and `organizationId`
- `POST /{id}/read` → `204 No Content` (or `404`)
- `POST /read-all` → `204 No Content` (current user + organization only)

## Kafka events consumed
- Topic: `organization.events`
- Consumer group: `srv-notification`
- Event: `organization.member.added`

```json
{
  "eventId": "guid",
  "eventType": "organization.member.added",
  "occurredAt": "2026-08-07T10:15:00Z",
  "organizationId": "guid",
  "organizationName": "Acme Corp",
  "userId": "guid",
  "addedByUserId": "guid",
  "roleIds": ["guid"]
}
```

- Sources: organization member add + invitation accept (via transactional outbox)
- Idempotency: unique `eventId` on `user_notifications`
- Storage: PostgreSQL `notification_db` (Aspire) / `notificationdb` (staging Compose)

## Frontend
- Org-scoped: `/app/organizations/:slug/notifications` (member-only, same access as chat)
- Hub tile on `/app/organizations/:slug`
- `NotificationService` → `GET /organizations/{organizationId}`
- Mark read uses `POST /organizations/{organizationId}/{id}/read` and `POST /organizations/{organizationId}/read-all`

## Don't
- Do not call organization HTTP from notification for this flow (event-driven only).
